{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_011Cf6JqE4HSyd2pRdHg5mdP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done! I've added the new endpoint following the existing architecture and patterns. Here are the files I changed:\n\n**Changed files:**\n1. **src/tags/repository.ts** - Added `listPopular()` method that queries the database for the top 10 tags ordered by article count descending\n2. **src/tags/service.ts** - Added `listPopular()` method that wraps the repository call\n3. **src/tags/routes.ts** - Added GET `/tags/popular` route handler\n\nThe endpoint is now available at **GET /api/tags/popular** (the `/api` prefix comes from the router registration in `app.ts`).\n\nThe implementation:\n- Returns exactly 10 tags (or fewer if there aren't 10 tags with articles)\n- Orders by usage count (most-used first)\n- Returns JSON in the exact shape requested: `{ \"tags\": [{ \"name\": \"<tag>\", \"count\": <number> }] }`\n- Follows the existing error handling pattern (422 status on failure)\n- Uses Prisma's `_count` feature to efficiently aggregate article counts\n- Only includes tags that have at least one article (matching the existing `list()` behavior)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":483,"cache_read_input_tokens":33505,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":483},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2348eff4-70c4-4a2d-8a32-398bd3687eca","uuid":"c9515491-c18c-40a3-a230-b885c0034f6d","timestamp":"2026-09-16T02:12:22.680Z","request_id":"req_011Cf6JqDhhBbSbuTKkF5cn9"}
